    "claim": "Store meta.json cargo dependencies are the source the builder regenerates crate Cargo.tomls from - bumping a crate version in a Cargo.toml without updating the owning library's store meta makes every subsequent rebuild silently regress it. The 2026-08-09 flowlang 0.3.31 / ndata 0.3.17 sync had this latent regression via data/app/meta.json (still 0.3.30/0.3.16, masked by Cargo.lock semver compatibility); fixed via save_library_config on the nebula-overhaul branch. Corollary: dev.dev.compile on a newbound_core-rooted library builds only the newbound_core package as an error check - the host binary relink is a separate explicit `cargo build` at the checkout root, per the interim-process restart table.",
    "tags": "platform-api,build,meta.json,cargo,drift",
    "source": {
